	doi = {10.1063/1.98799},
	abstract = {A novel electroluminescent device is constructed using organic materials as the emitting elements. The diode has a double‐layer structure of organic thin films, prepared by vapor deposition. Efficient injection of holes and electrons is provided from an indium‐tin‐oxide anode and an alloyed Mg:Ag cathode. Electron‐hole recombination and green electroluminescent emission are confined near the organic interface region. High external quantum efficiency (1\% photon/electron), luminous efficiency (1.5 lm/W), and brightness (\&gt;1000 cd/m2) are achievable at a driving voltage below 10 V.},
